Atlas overlay patch 0106: ui/kit-sidebar-pane
Why: with the Kit chrome the tab sidebar is a view of our own inside the engine's vertical tab strip region, and the
 engine's F6 (pane focus) list names the region, which has nothing visible to focus once the engine's own strip is
 hidden: F6 cycled toolbar and page and never reached the sidebar (ATLAS-E2E-15; the sidebar was reachable only by
 Tab). BrowserView::GetAccessiblePanes names the Kit sidebar in place of the region when it is there; the sidebar
 puts focus on the row of the tab in front (KitSidebarView::RequestFocus). Off unless --atlas-kit-chrome.
Files: chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_view.cc
Test filter: AtlasKit (journey e2e_keys_hover.py: F6 x4 visits the sidebar)
Rebase risk: L (one branch in a list of panes; kit_chrome.h is already included by patch 0100)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series and patch 0100 applied (dev slot 8)

--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_view.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_view.cc
@@ -5219,7 +5219,12 @@
     panes->push_back(horizontal_tab_strip_region_view_);
   }
   if (vertical_tab_strip_region_view_) {
-    panes->push_back(vertical_tab_strip_region_view_);
+    // Atlas: with the Kit chrome the sidebar itself is the pane, so F6 lands
+    // on its rows (the engine's region has nothing visible to focus).
+    views::View* kit_sidebar =
+        atlas::kit::KitSidebarOf(vertical_tab_strip_region_view_);
+    panes->push_back(kit_sidebar ? kit_sidebar
+                                 : vertical_tab_strip_region_view_.get());
   }
   if (toolbar_ && toolbar_->custom_tab_bar()) {
     panes->push_back(toolbar_->custom_tab_bar());
